ELISCRIPT RUNTIME LIBRARY EXCEPTION

Version 1.0, 26 November 2026

Everyone is permitted to copy and distribute verbatim copies of this
license document, but changing it is not allowed.

This Eliscript Runtime Library Exception ("Exception") is an additional
permission under section 7 of the GNU General Public License, version 3
("GPLv3", see LICENSE). It applies to a given file, runtime module,
standard-library module, platform capability adapter, browser host/loader,
or generated support artifact (the "Runtime Library") that bears a notice
placed by the copyright holder stating that the work is governed by GPLv3
(or any later version published by the Free Software Foundation) along with
this Exception.

When you use Eliscript to compile or execute a program, Eliscript may
combine, inline, bundle, or reference portions of Eliscript runtime modules,
standard-library modules, platform adapters, or browser loaders with the
compiled output. The purpose of this Exception is to allow non-GPL
(including proprietary and closed-source commercial) programs to use, bundle,
and distribute the covered Runtime Libraries and generated output, while
preserving GPLv3 copyleft over the Eliscript compiler and the Runtime
Libraries themselves.

0. Definitions.

A file or module is an "Independent Module" if it either requires the
Runtime Library for execution after a Compilation Process, or makes use of
an interface provided by the Runtime Library, but is not otherwise based on
the Runtime Library.

"Eliscript" means the Eliscript compiler and toolchain (including seed
compiler, self-hosted compiler, lowers, backends, and build tools), with or
without modifications, governed by version 3 (or any later version published
by the Free Software Foundation) of the GNU General Public License (GPL).

"GPL-compatible Software" is software whose conditions of propagation,
modification, and use would permit combination with Eliscript in accord with
the license of Eliscript.

"Target Code" refers to output from a compiler for a real or virtual target
execution environment, including ECMAScript/JavaScript modules, bundled
browser or host artifacts, WebAssembly bytecode/modules, and native object
code or executables. Notwithstanding that, Target Code does not include
data in any format that is used as a compiler intermediate representation
(IR), or used for producing a compiler intermediate representation.

The "Compilation Process" transforms code entirely represented in
non-intermediate languages designed for human-written code (including
Emacs Lisp and Eliscript `.eli` sources) into Target Code. Independent source
generators and preprocessors need not be considered part of the Compilation
Process, since the Compilation Process can be understood as starting with
the output of the generators or preprocessors.

A Compilation Process is "Eligible" if it is done using Eliscript, alone or
with other GPL-compatible Software, or if it is done without using any work
based on Eliscript. For example, using non-GPL-compatible Software to inspect
or optimize any Eliscript compiler intermediate representations (IR) would
not qualify as an Eligible Compilation Process.

1. Grant of Additional Permission.

You have permission to propagate a work of Target Code formed by combining
(including bundling, linking, importing, or inlining) the Runtime Library
with Independent Modules, even if such propagation would otherwise violate
the terms of GPLv3, provided that all Target Code was generated by Eligible
Compilation Processes. You may then convey such a combination under terms
of your choice, consistent with the licensing of the Independent Modules.

2. No Weakening of Eliscript Copyleft.

The availability of this Exception does not imply any general presumption
that third-party software is unaffected by the copyleft requirements of
the license of Eliscript. Modifications to, derivations from, and standalone
distributions of the Eliscript compiler/toolchain (`compiler/`,
`bootstrap/`, `tools/`) or of the covered Runtime Libraries themselves
remain fully governed by GPL-3.0-or-later.

3. Covered Runtime Libraries.

Subject to the notices in each directory and README, the following trees in
the Eliscript repository and their materialized package outputs are covered
by this Exception:

- `runtime/` and `dist/runtime/` (persistent data structures, Lisp runtime,
  value/wire codecs, worker streams)
- `stdlib/` and `dist/stdlib/` (standard library and portable modules)
- `platform/` (explicit browser, HTTP, and worker capability adapters)
- `browser/` and `dist/browser/` (in-memory compiler host wrapper, worker
  transport, and live script loader runtime bundled into applications)
- Any future Eliscript UI, macro, or application-support package that
  explicitly includes a notice incorporating this Exception
